// The corpus refresher's gate. The primary encoding gate over the
// seeded corpus is fuzz-corpus.test, which runs everywhere because the
// corpus is checked in; what this file guards — where uv exists — is
// that the checked-in corpus is exactly what the generator produces,
// so the ungated gate never quietly tests yesterday's neighborhood.
// The seed is fixed (oracle/fuzz.py SEED), so a divergence here means
// the generator or the model moved and the corpus must be re-minted
// with it:
//   uv --project reference run python -m oracle.fuzz mlir \
//     > test/Encoding/Inputs/fuzz-corpus.mlir
//   uv --project reference run python -m oracle.fuzz ids \
//     > test/Encoding/Inputs/fuzz-corpus.ids
// REQUIRES: uv
// RUN: %uv python -m oracle.fuzz mlir > %t.gen.mlir
// RUN: diff %t.gen.mlir %S/Inputs/fuzz-corpus.mlir
// RUN: %uv python -m oracle.fuzz ids > %t.want.ids
// RUN: diff %t.want.ids %S/Inputs/fuzz-corpus.ids
